subject: test(chatCore): regression test for onRequestSuccess guard (GAP-P1-05)

The .catch() on the onRequestSuccess promise chain already exists at HEAD
(upstream 0d216689, 2026-06-26) — the gap scan that spawned this card hit a
stale pre-merge snapshot. This adds a regression test so the guard cannot be
silently removed:

- onRequestSuccess is invoked on valid provider response (fire-and-forget)
- sync throw inside onRequestSuccess is contained: logged, handler resolves
- async rejection is contained by the chain .catch: logged, handler resolves
- success body returns intact even when onRequestSuccess fails

Anti-false-positive verified: intentionally breaking the logged-assertion
makes 2/4 tests fail; restoring returns to 4/4 pass.

